// PipAI - an autonomous digital pet with a real (tiny) neural-network brain.
// For the Waveshare ESP32-S3-ePaper-1.54 (V2).
//
// Every 90 seconds Pip senses its surroundings (temperature, humidity, time of day,
// battery, your pats) and its own needs, and its neural network - trained with
// reinforcement learning on GitHub - decides what to do. Each Pip is born with a
// random personality (curious, playful, lazy, brave, affectionate) that changes
// how it behaves. Everything runs on the board; no internet AI, no API keys.
//
// On screen Pip lives in a little room: it walks to its bed to nap, to its bowl
// to eat, into its box to hide, wanders when exploring, jumps when it plays,
// dances, and gazes out of the window.
//
// Every few minutes Pip says something in a speech bubble.
// Pip can also feel grumpy (woken up), sulky (ignored), scared (flipped / loud noises) or
// frustrated (can't do what it wants). Each feeling fades on its own; snacks and pats help.
//
// Buttons: tap BOOT to drop a snack, tap PWR to pet Pip (it hops). Hold BOOT 5 s to forget Wi-Fi.
// Phone: join "Pip-Setup" Wi-Fi the first time, then open http://pip.local
//
// Files: pip_world.h = Pip's world rules, pip_brain.h = the trained network
// (generated by training/train.py - don't edit by hand).

